WEBVTT

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.230
Senpai!

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.660
Senpai, sorry for making you worry!

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:19.910
Tsubasa-chan!

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.790
Will you accompany me?

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.290
Of course!

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.250
Hundred Flowers Type 8!

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.910
Petits Ciseaux!

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.910
Creeping Cherry Blossoms!

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:38.600
Gatcha!

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.280
The Infinite Blade, Storm!

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.450
The Right Hand of Death!

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.530
What's our good-for-nothing prime 
minister doing right now, anyway?

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:30.170
He should show himself at a time like this.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.010
<i>I'm talking to you, Gelsadra!</i>

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.590
<b>Gelsadra! Unforgivable! Take Responsibility!</b>

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:39.880
I don't want to disappear... 
I want to stay here forever.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:44.500
Sadly, that's not for you to decide.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.910
Let's leave the rest up to them.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.200
Just how many of these things are there?!

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.610
I'm gloomy.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.380
Why are you getting in the way, Gatchaman?

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.580
You guys seriously don't get it.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:12.420
It's futile. This atmosphere won't 
be gone until Gelsadra dies.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.320
Apes don't stop until they get bored.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.250
How long is this going to go on, Senpai?

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.850
Hmm...

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.940
What do you think, Katze-san?

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:33.030
That's simple. You just have 
to stop this atmosphere.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.500
Katze-san, how do you stop an atmosphere?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.950
Well, once everyone's satisfied, it'll stop. Duh.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.360
I see.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.030
Tsubasa-chan, what do you think?

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.630
Does that mean we have to defeat Gel-chan?

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.370
That won't resolve anything, though.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.850
Why's that?

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:59.170
Because it's not Gel-chan 
that's at fault. It's all of us.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.120
Good point.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.380
Here comes the goodie-goodie act.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.060
How long are you going to say 
delusional things like that?

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.310
You don't understand Atmosphere-chan at all.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:17.850
You and Gel-Gel got 
together and made it, too.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.190
That's exactly why I want to do 
something about this atmosphere.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.030
I want everyone to realize how scary it is.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.240
Nope! Nope, nope.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.700
This is the nope game. Everyone thinks 
they're right, so they won't back down.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.150
You're all so naive. So naive!

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:37.470
You all just want to see 
other people's misfortunes

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.590
for eternity.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.520
So your stupid festival continues 
because you all are Neanderthals.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.090
Lololol!

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.320
Well, see you next week!

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.180
The next episode will be 
"Gel Covered in Blood."

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.370
Bye-bye!

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.700
I see...

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.250
Bird Out.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.120
Senpai?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.230
Tsubasa-chan...

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:08.330
There's something off 
about the way we're fighting.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.860
Senpai, you can't mean...

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.500
It can't be helped.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.850
<b>Breaking news!</b>

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.000
Huh? Breaking news?

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:19.710
<b>Gelsadra is on the run!!</b>

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.800
This is an emergency! We just received 
word that Gelsadra is on the run!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.330
<i>This is unbelievable!</i>

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.120
<i>Oh, there's the breaking news update.</i>

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.690
<i>Gelsadra is on the run.</i>

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.350
Hey, it says Gelsadra's on the run.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.350
But where would he even run to?

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:42.320
<b>Breaking News: Gelsadra On The Run</b>

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:39.980
<i>What? He's the prime minister, 
and he's on the run?</i>

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:45.470
<i>Oh, that silly alien. How selfish.</i>

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.580
<i>For the time being, everyone 
in Tachikawa, please be careful.</i>

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.960
<i>He might try to take hostages 
while he's on the run!</i>

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.180
Oh, no! Save me, Kuu-sama!

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:56.280
<i>So scary! I wonder if he's going 
to run away in his space saucer.</i>

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.610
There, there. I'll beat him to a pulp.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.390
Prepare yourself, Grossadra!

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.790
<i>His ship should be broken. It's doubtful.</i>

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.130
Field Open.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.010
Hajime-chan! Rui-kun!

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:22.190
Sugayama-san?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.190
OD...

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:27.950
Oh, my... Nice to meet you...

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.110
DD-chan.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.780
Th-This is too sudden!

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.290
Hajime-chan, what's going on?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.580
We're going to do a smart phone poll.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.380
Smart phone poll? Of what?

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.930
Sugayan. It's up to you.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.430
Okay!

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:53.470
Everyone, this is sudden, 
but please get your smart phones ready.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:56.640
Currently, Gelsadra is on the run.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.780
In order to resolve this dangerous situation,

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.570
there is something I'd like to ask you.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:03.360
And that's...

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.980
Okay! Here's the question...

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.440
You guys ready?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.780
Would you like us Gatchaman 
to do something about Gelsadra?

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:16.950
I see! The Gatchaman are finally 
standing up for this country!

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.660
Hey, hurry with the preparations.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.250
All right! We're counting on your votes!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.070
Hey, what should we do?

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.180
Gelsadra's an alien, right?

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.350
I'm gonna go again!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.800
Then, that means...

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.760
<b>Right?  Nope!
Leave it to Gatchaman</b>

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.590
X, I'm counting on you.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:35.210
As you wish.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.560
<b>Leave it to Gatchaman</b>

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.560
<b>Right!</b>

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.560
<b>Nope!</b>

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:39.060
And the results are in! So fast!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:45.520
Got it. Then the Gatchaman will take 
responsibility and do something about it.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:46.980
All right?

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.640
That's our Gatchaman! So reliable.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.520
You think you're so slick.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.910
Because I am.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.810
So that's their move.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.860
But this doesn't change the result 
of seeing blood in the end.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.340
I'm gloomy...

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.280
Bite and...

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.680
What got into them all of a sudden?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.970
I'm gloomy.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:27.360
Gatcha! Gatcha! Gatcha! Gatcha!

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.890
Don't come any closer!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.680
Man, the Gatchaman always 
save the day in the end!

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.100
Jou-san!

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.480
Thanks, Jou-san!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.720
Jou-san, what was that?

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.110
The atmosphere changed again.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:38.640
Go, go, Gatchaman!

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.390
Go, go, Gatcha! Go, go, Gatcha!

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.510
Gatcha!

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.390
Gatcha!

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:43.200
Gatcha!

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.290
Oh, Jou-san. Do that Phoenix Dive!

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:53.970
Phoenix Dive! Phoenix Dive!

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.970
You guys sure change your tune easily.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.930
This is the only way to save everyone.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.560
Got it?

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.890
All right, here we go!

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.190
Gatcha!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.400
We're gonna kill Gel-chan!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:22.330
<b>Tokyo Tachikawa</b>

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:22.330
<b>Tense Battle: Gatchaman vs Gelsadra</b>

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.740
<i>One day has passed since</i>

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.330
<i>the decision was made that the 
Gatchaman would deal with Gelsadra.</i>

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.860
<i>It can truly be said that Tachikawa 
is in the calm before the st...</i>

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.330
B-Behind you! Behind you!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:28.160
It's Gelsadra! Gelsadra 
has appeared in Tachikawa!

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.760
Save us, Gatchaman!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.540
Hey! It's Gelsadra!

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.680
Hurry, Gatchaman!

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:35.970
Sadra has appeared!

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.590
Fight, my fragments!

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.020
Stop running, Sadra!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.850
Gatchaman!

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.030
Digitize!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.080
X-saucer!

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:46.580
Bite and Build!

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.750
You're not getting away!

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.200
Burning Rain!

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.540
Burning Hammer!

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.540
Volcano!

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:40.170
This is amazing.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.260
He's so hot and...

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:47.010
<b>Tokyo Tachikawa</b>

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:53.400
<b>Huge Clash! You Can Do It, Heroes!!</b>

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.580
<i>too amazing!</i>

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.010
<i>How are they even filming this?</i>

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:50.980
<i>Um... It appears that 
the security cameras in the area</i>

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.400
<i>are streaming this live on the Internet.</i>

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.980
This is Maiasa TV! 
We would love to get that footage.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.980
This is Tokiwa TV! 
Please give your footage to us!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.150
If possible, could we get 
the exclusive broadcast?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:04.220
<i>I think we can just keep going 
with the Internet streaming.</i>

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.980
<i>It's so exciting!</i>

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:10.870
<i>We just connected with our reporter, Saito, 
who's on the scene at Hanamidori Park.</i>

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:11.830
<i>Saito-san.</i>

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:17.540
<i>Yes. I'm here right in front of the 
still-peaceful Blue Sky Cabinet Hall.</i>

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:29.140
Gatcha! Gatcha!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.480
Hey! Whadya think you're doing, stupid Sadra.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:59.460
Get 'em, Gatchaman! Beat that gross alien!

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.120
Hey, hurry!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:22.860
Gelsadra just ran into Hanamidori Park 
barely hanging onto his life!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:27.720
Take this!

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.940
Up Down!

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.620
Creeping Cherry Blossoms!

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.710
Go! Do it!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.430
Take that, Sadra.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.150
Yeah!

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.930
Gatcha's awesome!

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.850
Rending Gale Blade!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.010
Holy crap, Gatcha.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.820
They sure aren't holding back.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:13.200
Just give up already, Sadra.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.890
Die, Sadra.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.880
I'll roast you with the flames of justice.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:26.790
Phoenix Dive!

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:41.220
Come on, now...

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.250
This is going too far...

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.190
Isn't that enough?

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.490
They couldn't possibly...

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.450
<b>Dictator Sadra on the Brink of Death?! Gatchaman Have the Upper Hand!!</b>

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.290
This is a bit...

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.570
This is going entirely too far...

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.840
We're getting a ton of complaints?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.160
Let's stop the broadcast for a sec!

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.620
Turn it back to the studio!

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.770
<b>......... 
 This isn't funny 
 We never said take it this far</b>

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:21.690
<b>So, where's Hajime-tan? 
 Did she run?</b>

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:34.240
Prepare yourself, you ugly monster.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.560
Go forth to your eternal slumber.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.450
Take this final blow!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.580
Please stop!

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.080
This is more than enough!

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.460
You're in the way! Move!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.170
No!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.320
The Infinite Blade, Storm!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:52.860
Huh?

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.970
Hang in there. Hang in there.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.430
Everyone, please look.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.570
<i>I wonder if Grossadra was properly buried.</i>

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:21.470
<i>Who knows?</i>

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.770
<i>But it's only been a day.</i>

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.130
<i>Who cares about Sadra?</i>

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.170
<i>Yeah, I was taken aback.</i>

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.520
<i>Isn't there something 
more funny on the news?</i>

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.160
It looks like our plan was a success for now.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.530
But what's important 
is what will happen now.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.660
I've made arrangements with Millio-chan.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.190
I'll go.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:43.240
I made a promise to Senpai.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:48.270
Senpai, leave the rest to us.

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:54.890
Good job, Gatcha!

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.170
Gel-Gel was so annoying.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.800
But you guys might've gone a bit overboard.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:00.800
Shut up!

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:03.990
You were the ones who left it up to us!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.710
Now, we have Tsubasa-chan here 
representing the Gatchaman,

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:21.890
and she has an important announcement.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:22.660
Yes.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.870
Everyone, please listen carefully.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.310
Gelsadra is

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.260
<i>alive.</i>

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.260
<b>Breaking News: Gatchaman Have an Important Announcement! 
Misudachi Tsubasa Live in Studio!</b>

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.140
Huh?

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.920
Sadra's alive?

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.140
What does she mean?

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.600
Hajime-chan, I'm so sorry.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:51.480
Gelsadra was never on the run.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:54.410
We, the Gatchaman, had him in custody.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:01.280
We're sorry. We had 
no intention of deceiving you.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:06.200
<i>This is something that we all, 
as Gatchaman, decided together.</i>

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.730
But Sadra was totally there.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.920
He was totally getting his butt kicked.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:11.750
Right?

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:22.690
There's something off 
about the way we're fighting.

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:28.230
And then, Senpai called out to us.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.770
We're about to have a smart phone poll.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.950
She said that this was a matter 
that affected all of us

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.570
so we should ask everyone.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.870
<b>Leave it to Gatchaman</b>

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.870
<b>Right!</b>

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.870
<b>Nope!</b>

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:51.620
Got it. Then the Gatchaman will take 
responsibility and do something about it.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.080
All right?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.980
But, Hajime-chan, what are 
you guys actually going to do?

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.800
We're gonna go discuss that now.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:04.260
And so, we had a discussion

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.900
on what we should do about Gelsadra.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:13.060
Hajime-senpai's proposal was 
more than we could have ever imagined.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:15.060
Kill Gelsadra?

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:19.670
Yep! This atmosphere won't 
calm down until everyone's satisfied.

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:20.690
Senpai!

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.280
Of course, I was against it.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.810
We didn't have to kill him. 
We could just send him back to his planet.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.650
But...

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.700
That's not going to work. This is a chance.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.920
A chance? A chance for what?

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.380
For all of us to know just who we really are.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:44.240
Senpai told us that our enemy this time 
wasn't the Kuu-samas or Gelsadra...

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.260
That it was actually all of us,

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:50.470
and the atmosphere that we all created.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.190
This is a more difficult opponent 
than we've ever faced before.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:58.090
We might not be able to defeat it, 
but we can at least make everyone aware.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:02.530
We can't just keep letting something 
so ambiguous like the atmosphere

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:04.990
that can change in an instant 
keep controlling us.

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:08.130
That's why we're going 
to stop the atmosphere,

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:10.950
and she said we're going 
to kill Gelsadra to do it.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.150
Everyone will be satisfied if Gel-chan dies.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:18.700
Actually, they'll be so satisfied that 
they'll stop talking about it all together.

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:22.310
Otherwise, this atmosphere won't stop.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:23.910
But I don't want that!

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:29.350
It'll be fine, Tsubasa-chan. 
If all of us work together.

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:31.310
All of us...

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:35.800
But Hajime-chan wasn't at the battle, right?

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.980
No, Senpai was there...

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.500
Right in the center of that battle.
